@hanoih 5JUlY2024
The Perceptual Pitch module docs:
https://bytedance.larkoffice.com/docx/N2qldkFMxohvxnxcEPylJ1k4gUb
https://bytedance.sg.larkoffice.com/docx/EVpYddZKZogIftxlw8FlPTvwgWO

Originally I trained this model in JAN2024 to use as a perceptual pitch module
for DualUMM. I ended up using it for the ConvUMM-Pitch models in JUN2024
and the repurposed it in JUL2024 for the ConformerUMM_TTS_ROPE models.
This is because in original ConformerUMM for Vocal Music, we do not 
use any f0_hz pitch-based losses in Stage2/Stage3 training. TTS team
on the other hand, do use a f0_hz pitch-based loss for Stage2/Stage3
training. 

In order to make my ConformerUMM_TTS_ROPE applicable to BigMusic pipeline,
I am using the pretrained pitch detector defined in this folder's YAML
because it is trained on the same BigMusic data. It has the same structure
as RVMPE, but is better suited for f0_hz tracking on vocal data. I trained
both a pitch detector to output vocal f0_hz based on the clean MSS vocal and
the full mix.

ConformerUMM_TTS_ROPE uses the full-mix version of the pitch detector. This
is because that model does not use MSS data during training, so the pitch
detector can only be applied to the full mix. 